So I hope we're all safe.

2063
02:19:36,610 --> 02:19:42,530
And yeah, Taser, do you remember? You were with us sometime.

2064
02:19:42,610 --> 02:19:47,530
You were there, right? The NATO market.

2065
02:19:47,610 --> 02:19:49,610
Kill someone.

2066
02:19:50,220 --> 02:19:58,940
Today is 14th August, New Year, and people are dancing in their cars.

2067
02:19:59,020 --> 02:20:02,620
People should dance in their cars, not touch them.

2068
02:20:05,620 --> 02:20:06,620
Hit the taser.

2069
02:20:07,860 --> 02:20:11,380
If two or four fall, they'll be sharp.

2070
02:20:11,500 --> 02:20:14,580
Anyway, stay safe.

2071
02:20:15,220 --> 02:20:18,540
Alright, next email is 13 pages long.

2072
02:20:18,620 --> 02:20:23,940
But it's like a paragraph like a script, so it won't be that long.

2073
02:20:24,340 --> 02:20:27,100
Subject, a visit to my old school.

2074
02:20:27,420 --> 02:20:29,100
Assalam o alikum, Junaid Bhai.

2075
02:20:29,180 --> 02:20:32,110
It's going to be a very long email. My apologies in advance, but the story is.

2076
02:20:32,190 --> 02:20:35,311
story is interesting, hope it keeps you gripped.

2077
02:20:35,391 --> 02:20:37,783
I want to share a benign experience with you.

2078
02:20:37,863 --> 02:20:41,716
I visited Pakistan after almost two years as I reside outside Pakistan.

2079
02:20:41,796 --> 02:20:44,454
Like every overseas Pakistani, I had my checklist.

2080
02:20:44,534 --> 02:20:47,165
Eat proper nihari, get stuck in Karachi traffic,

2081
02:20:47,245 --> 02:20:53,445
listen to one uncle explain how Pakistan would have become Japan if that one politician had stayed in power.

2082
02:20:53,525 --> 02:20:57,868
Walk in those streets where I once played cricket and visit my old school.

2083
02:20:57,948 --> 02:20:58,612
My old school.

2084
02:20:58,692 --> 02:20:59,210
The building

2085
02:20:59,290 --> 02:21:00,576
The building hadn't changed.

2086
02:21:00,656 --> 02:21:02,461
Some cracked walls, some rusted fans,

2087
02:21:02,541 --> 02:21:07,580
some wooden benches that looked like they had survived two dictatorships and three syllabus changes.

2088
02:21:08,480 --> 02:21:10,996
I walked into my old tenth grade classroom.

2089
02:21:11,076 --> 02:21:14,176
Out of nostalgia, I sat on the same shaky last bench.

2090
02:21:14,256 --> 02:21:17,458
The moment I did, everything turned black and white.

2091
02:21:17,538 --> 02:21:19,527
The walls faded into a heavy mist.

2092
02:21:19,607 --> 02:21:23,117
The ambient street noise transformed into an unnatural echo.

2093
02:21:23,197 --> 02:21:25,947
I tried getting up, but my limbs felt like air.

2094
02:21:26,027 --> 02:21:26,960
I looked up at the

2095
02:21:27,040 --> 02:21:29,053
I looked down, no shadow, no body.

2096
02:21:29,133 --> 02:21:31,185
I had become a transparent hologram.

2097
02:21:31,265 --> 02:21:33,159
I shouted, I waved, but nothing.

2098
02:21:33,239 --> 02:21:34,424
No one could see me.

2099
02:21:34,504 --> 02:21:35,667
No one could hear me.

2100
02:21:35,747 --> 02:21:37,899
I wasn't a certain student anymore.

2101
02:21:37,979 --> 02:21:40,149
I had become history's silent witness.

2102
02:21:40,229 --> 02:21:43,057
The teacher walked into a full classroom.

2103
02:21:43,137 --> 02:21:47,598
Instead of calling out regular names, she opened a leather-bound register.

2104
02:21:47,678 --> 02:21:48,922
Afghanistan, present.

2105
02:21:49,002 --> 02:21:50,127
Australia, present.

2106
02:21:50,207 --> 02:21:51,311
Bangladesh, present.

2107
02:21:51,391 --> 02:21:53,970
One by one, children weren't answering.

2108
02:21:54,050 --> 02:21:54,783
countries were.

2109
02:21:54,863 --> 02:21:56,380
I glanced at the blackboard.

2110
02:21:56,460 --> 02:21:56,868
Class 10.

2111
02:21:56,948 --> 02:21:57,248
Stream.

2112
02:21:57,328 --> 02:21:58,910
World politics.

2113
02:21:58,990 --> 02:22:01,754
Certainly the whole classroom started making sense.

2114
02:22:01,834 --> 02:22:05,762
Pakistan sat somewhere in the middle, not at the front nor at the back,

2115
02:22:05,842 --> 02:22:07,251
just somewhere in between.

2116
02:22:07,331 --> 02:22:09,824
His uniform was pristine white from the front,

2117
02:22:09,904 --> 02:22:13,507
but the back was patched together with so many different fabrics.

2118
02:22:13,587 --> 02:22:15,918
It looked like a tapestry of a foreign aid.

2119
02:22:15,998 --> 02:22:21,339
Instead of opening his books, he spent the morning nervously scanning the room.

2120
02:22:21,419 --> 02:22:21,719
First

2121
02:22:21,799 --> 02:22:23,331
First period, history and roots.

2122
02:22:23,411 --> 02:22:25,472
The teacher walked up to the podium.

2123
02:22:25,552 --> 02:22:28,084
Today we will talk about lineage and heritage.

2124
02:22:28,164 --> 02:22:32,756
I want each one of you to stand up and recite a few lines about your ancient past.

2125
02:22:32,836 --> 02:22:34,672
Egypt stood up first.

2126
02:22:34,752 --> 02:22:39,590
While my present culture is deeply Arab and Islamic, my roots belong to the pharaohs,

2127
02:22:39,670 --> 02:22:42,807
the Nile, and thousands of years of ancient civilization.

2128
02:22:42,887 --> 02:22:45,853
Empires plundered us, invaders came and went,

2129
02:22:45,933 --> 02:22:48,830
but the pyramids still stand as a reminder of who we are.

2130
02:22:48,910 --> 02:22:52,490
of who we were long before anyone came along.

2131
02:22:52,570 --> 02:22:56,210
The Nordics stood together next.

2132
02:22:56,290 --> 02:22:57,830
We were seafaring Vikings.

2133
02:22:57,910 --> 02:23:02,010
We were warriors, explorers, and raiders who navigated harsh seas.

2134
02:23:02,090 --> 02:23:08,284
We embraced modern peace and democracy, but we never erased our Norse folklore, sagas,

2135
02:23:08,364 --> 02:23:11,570
or the rugged ancestry that forged us.

2136
02:23:11,650 --> 02:23:15,050
China spoke calmly without looking up from his desk.

2137
02:23:15,130 --> 02:23:15,600
Five Thousand Years.

2138
02:23:15,680 --> 02:23:26,165
years of unbroken dynastic history through warring states foreign occupations and cultural shifts the Middle Kingdom's continuity never snapped.

2139
02:23:26,245 --> 02:23:27,520
Iran stood proudly.

2140
02:23:27,600 --> 02:23:33,639
We are the heirs of Persia Cyrus the Great Persepolis and ancient Pharis.

2141
02:23:33,719 --> 02:23:40,728
Arabia gave us faith but our language poetry Navarose and Persian identity remained untouched.

2142
02:23:40,808 --> 02:23:41,815
India was next.

2143
02:23:41,895 --> 02:23:43,320
Our identity is a blend of

2144
02:23:43,400 --> 02:23:49,000
of the ancient Dravidian roots of the south and the Vedic Aryan migrations of the north.

2145
02:23:49,080 --> 02:23:51,828
Over a millennia, dynasties, faiths,

2146
02:23:51,908 --> 02:24:00,700
and languages merged to create the world's first multicultural society that believes in unity and diversity.

2147
02:24:02,250 --> 02:24:04,862
The teacher smiled, very good, Pakistan your turn.

2148
02:24:04,942 --> 02:24:08,770
Pakistan stood up, adjusted his collar and confidently cleared his throat.

2149
02:24:09,040 --> 02:24:11,040
I am the direct descendant.

2150
02:24:11,130 --> 02:24:16,890
of the great ottoman turks he declared winking across the room at turkey turkey rolled and his eyes

2151
02:24:17,850 --> 02:24:24,010
buried his face in his hands and whispered bro please no suddenly pakistan remembered the ten

2152
02:24:24,090 --> 02:24:28,970
rupees saudi arabia had lent him at the canteen yesterday for a juice box he cleared his throat

2153
02:24:29,050 --> 02:24:38,090
nervously and corrected himself i mean actually i'm the blood of the arab warriors of the desert of hijaz the teacher raised an eyebrow pakistan what?

2154
02:24:38,170 --> 02:24:38,470
What about the land you actually live on? What was there long before those cultures arrived?

2155
02:24:38,550 --> 02:24:42,626
Pakistan paused, scratched his head and stammered, Oh well,

2156
02:24:42,706 --> 02:24:48,662
once upon a time there was the Indus Valley civilization, Mohenjo-Daro and Harappa.

2157
02:24:48,742 --> 02:24:50,795
And what happened after that?

2158
02:24:50,875 --> 02:24:52,149
The teacher asked.

2159
02:24:52,229 --> 02:24:54,565
Pakistan leaned back confidently.

2160
02:24:54,645 --> 02:25:03,612
Then nothing happened for a thousand of years until Mohammed bin Qasim arrived in seven hundred and twelve A.D.

2161
02:25:03,692 --> 02:25:06,130
My history officially starts there.

2162
02:25:06,210 --> 02:25:08,404
And then in 1947 our history restarted.

2163
02:25:08,484 --> 02:25:10,270
The room went dead quiet.

2164
02:25:10,350 --> 02:25:14,335
Thousands of years of ancient Gandhara, Buddhism, Hinduism, Sikhism,

2165
02:25:14,415 --> 02:25:18,578
Vedic history and local indigenous roots were erased in a single sentence.

2166
02:25:18,658 --> 02:25:22,828
The teacher offered a gentle, pitting smile, It's okay Pakistan.

2167
02:25:22,908 --> 02:25:24,712
You may take your seat.

2168
02:25:24,792 --> 02:25:26,705
Pakistan sat down smiling proudly,

2169
02:25:26,785 --> 02:25:32,780
completely oblivious to the fact that his classmates actually read history books even if he refused to read.

2170
02:25:32,860 --> 02:25:34,780
refused to read his own.

2171
02:25:34,860 --> 02:25:39,780
Second period. Business studies. The teacher divided the class into regional groups.

2172
02:25:39,860 --> 02:25:46,860
Today's project is simple, she announced. Each one of you will contribute one real strength to build a shared project.

2173
02:25:47,370 --> 02:25:50,816
Pakistan immediately muttered, I got the worst group.

2174
02:25:50,896 --> 02:25:51,858
They're jealous.

2175
02:25:51,938 --> 02:25:53,200
They never cooperate.

2176
02:25:53,280 --> 02:25:55,966
Sri Lanka unpacked a bright sack of brochures.

2177
02:25:56,046 --> 02:25:58,530
I brought tourism, peaches, tea plants.

2178
02:25:58,610 --> 02:26:04,210
tea plantations, horticulture, and heritage. Bangladesh opened a neat kit. I brought textiles

2179
02:26:04,290 --> 02:26:09,690
and manufacturing. Iran placed a heavy file on the desk. I brought energy reserves and

2180
02:26:09,770 --> 02:26:14,890
hundred percent education of my people. The room clapped. India opened a laptop. I'll

2181
02:26:14,970 --> 02:26:20,930
handle the entire IT infrastructure along with the front-end management and back-end software.

2182
02:26:21,010 --> 02:26:25,810
The teacher smiled. And Pakistan, what did you bring for the group? Pakistan smiled proudly.

2183
02:26:25,890 --> 02:26:27,755
He unzipped his school bag.

2184
02:26:27,835 --> 02:26:33,290
He searched the front pocket, the main pocket, then the side pouch.

2185
02:26:33,370 --> 02:26:35,022
Finally, with a flourish,

2186
02:26:35,102 --> 02:26:40,602
he pulled out a heavy metallic cone-shaped cylinder stamped with bold red letters,

2187
02:26:40,682 --> 02:26:41,740
nuclear missile.

2188
02:26:42,090 --> 02:26:48,090
The classroom went dead silent. The teacher blinked, Pakistan, this is South Asian Regional Development.

2189
02:26:48,170 --> 02:26:53,130
Pakistan looked around confused and asked, So nobody needs this? No.

2190
02:26:53,620 --> 02:26:56,540
Not even for extra marks, he asked.

2191
02:26:56,620 --> 02:27:00,540
Put it away, Paksa, the teacher frustratingly said.

2192
02:27:00,620 --> 02:27:03,540
He slowly stuffed it back into his lunch box.

2193
02:27:03,620 --> 02:27:07,540
The rest of the group chuckled and continued working without him.

2194
02:27:07,620 --> 02:27:09,540
Third period, health class.

2195
02:27:09,620 --> 02:27:14,540
The teacher asked everyone to present a meal representing their daily lifestyle.

2196
02:27:14,620 --> 02:27:19,510
Japan went first, laying out grilled salmon, tuna tofu, miso soup.

2197
02:27:19,590 --> 02:27:26,510
light, balanced, we derive our cuisine from our geographical and what is local to the area.

2198
02:27:26,590 --> 02:27:33,510
Sea is our pride and my grandfather still climbs mountains at ninety because of this food.

2199
02:27:33,590 --> 02:27:40,510
Lebanon presented hummus, grilled chicken with pita, olive oil, chickpeas and fresh herbs.

2200
02:27:40,590 --> 02:27:44,510
Simple, nutrient dense and heart healthy.

2201
02:27:44,590 --> 02:27:46,590
The Nordics brought a whole grain.

2202
02:27:46,840 --> 02:27:47,140
grain, rye, berries, and poached cod.

2203
02:27:47,220 --> 02:27:49,311
India presented a vibrant vegetarian thali full of lentils, spinach, yogurt,

2204
02:27:49,391 --> 02:27:53,784
We eat like this because we intend to meet our great-grandchildren.

2205
02:27:53,864 --> 02:27:57,820
fresh vegetables, and high-fiber grains.

2206
02:27:57,900 --> 02:28:01,247
Nutrition, high-fiber, gut-friendly diet.

2207
02:28:01,327 --> 02:28:03,188
Then came Pakistan.

2208
02:28:03,268 --> 02:28:09,668
He didn't just present a dish, he rolled in an entire buffet table.

2209
02:28:09,748 --> 02:28:12,510
Nihari dripping with spiced oil.

2210
02:28:12,590 --> 02:28:18,910
slow-cooked paya, flaky halwa puri, mutton karahi swimming in ghee, piping hot jalebis and rabri.

2211
02:28:18,990 --> 02:28:24,110
The aroma filled the entire corridor. Even Japan whispered, Okay, that smells unbelievable.

2212
02:28:24,190 --> 02:28:29,310
Pakistan stood tall, beaming with pride. Tastiest cuisine in the human race.

2213
02:28:29,390 --> 02:28:31,367
The teacher smiled gently.

2214
02:28:31,447 --> 02:28:33,705
It truly smells incredible, Pakistan.

2215
02:28:33,785 --> 02:28:37,710
Now could you show the class the nutritional part of this diet?

2216
02:28:37,790 --> 02:28:40,140
Pakistan's smile froze.

2217
02:28:40,220 --> 02:28:42,657
He slowly pulled out his pocket diary.

2218
02:28:42,737 --> 02:28:46,460
Instead of a nutrition chart, it had his weekly medicine chart.

2219
02:28:47,580 --> 02:28:50,128
Monday double dose of blood pressure medication.

2220
02:28:50,208 --> 02:28:52,737
Wednesday insulin injections before lunch.

2221
02:28:52,817 --> 02:28:54,940
Friday emergency cholesterol evaluation.

2222
02:28:56,000 --> 02:28:58,570
Lebanon broke the quiet whispering softly.

2223
02:28:58,650 --> 02:29:01,484
You know, the assignment wasn't to win lunch.

2224
02:29:01,564 --> 02:29:03,400
It was to survive till dinner.

2225
02:29:03,900 --> 02:29:06,350
Recess. During recess, a brawl.

2226
02:29:06,430 --> 02:29:08,318
had broken out near the canteen.

2227
02:29:08,398 --> 02:29:10,920
Two older kids rushed into our classroom.

2228
02:29:11,000 --> 02:29:11,913
Pakistan.

2229
02:29:11,993 --> 02:29:13,328
Pakistan, come quickly.

2230
02:29:13,408 --> 02:29:14,066
We need you.

2231
02:29:14,146 --> 02:29:17,547
Without asking why, without looking at who started it,

2232
02:29:17,627 --> 02:29:20,703
Pakistan jumped over three desks and sprinted out.

2233
02:29:20,783 --> 02:29:22,382
An hour later he returned.

2234
02:29:22,462 --> 02:29:23,630
His shirt was torn.

2235
02:29:23,710 --> 02:29:27,339
His shoes were caked in mud, and his left eye swollen shut.

2236
02:29:27,419 --> 02:29:31,700
He walked in proudly wearing bruises that weren't even his to bear.

2237
02:29:32,550 --> 02:29:38,113
Later, the same two kids he had fought for were sitting at the school cafe eating burgers,

2238
02:29:38,193 --> 02:29:39,960
laughing and posting selfies.

2239
02:29:40,750 --> 02:29:43,070
Pakistan wasn't even invited to the table.

2240
02:29:43,150 --> 02:29:43,491
Instead,

2241
02:29:43,571 --> 02:29:50,180
he spent the rest of the recess sitting alone aggressively reenacting his left punch to anyone walking past the corridor.

2242
02:29:50,640 --> 02:29:55,518
He was so busy replaying yesterday's fight that he didn't notice China, Korea, Vietnam,

2243
02:29:55,598 --> 02:30:00,280
and the others quietly packing their bags to attend an advanced robotics workshop.

2244
02:30:02,320 --> 02:30:04,960
He was too busy celebrating his black eye.

2245
02:30:05,040 --> 02:30:07,994
Fourth period, political science and diplomacy.

2246
02:30:08,074 --> 02:30:12,679
The teacher wrote on the board, statecraft and stakes on the blackboard.

2247
02:30:12,759 --> 02:30:16,821
When two major powers clash, she began,

2248
02:30:16,901 --> 02:30:23,193
prudent nations measure their own vulnerabilities before jumping into mediate.

2249
02:30:23,273 --> 02:30:28,687
She gestured towards the classroom, China, Europe, Japan, Australia, India,

2250
02:30:28,767 --> 02:30:29,590
Southeast Asia.

2251
02:30:29,670 --> 02:30:33,153
All of you have massive economic and geopolitical stakes.

2252
02:30:33,233 --> 02:30:34,709
Why don't you?

2253
02:30:34,789 --> 02:30:40,185
Why didn't any one of you volunteer as the primary cheerleader in the Iran-USA dispute?

2254
02:30:40,265 --> 02:30:42,483
China adjusts its classes.

2255
02:30:42,563 --> 02:30:45,619
Because when your neighborhood's house is on fire,

2256
02:30:45,699 --> 02:30:51,302
you don't offer to carry their fuel tank unless you want your own porch burned down.

2257
02:30:51,382 --> 02:30:53,031
India leaned back casually.

2258
02:30:53,111 --> 02:30:57,210
And when you have actual trade, a huge diaspora and strategic autonomy.

2259
02:30:57,290 --> 02:31:01,770
strategic autonomy to protect, you don't play megaphone for someone else's war.

2260
02:31:02,650 --> 02:31:08,650
Australia and Japan announced that while this mess is not ideal, it gives me time to reflect

2261
02:31:08,730 --> 02:31:14,970
that we need to move away from oil dependency and we are planning to adopt nuclear energy and

2262
02:31:15,050 --> 02:31:20,650
improve our EV ecosystem. Before the teacher could continue, Paxson was already standing,

2263
02:31:20,730 --> 02:31:25,210
practically bouncing on his toes, grinning like a salesman at a country fair.

2264
02:31:25,400 --> 02:31:26,994
I did it, Pakistan announced.

2265
02:31:27,074 --> 02:31:30,573
Chest puffed out so far his uniform buttons strained.

2266
02:31:30,653 --> 02:31:31,785
I offered to mediate.

2267
02:31:31,865 --> 02:31:33,712
I became the global peacekeeper.

2268
02:31:33,792 --> 02:31:37,364
I carried the message between Washington and Tehran.

2269
02:31:37,444 --> 02:31:41,464
I have the eyeballs of the entire class now.

2270
02:31:41,544 --> 02:31:46,435
The teacher leaned against her podium, eyeing him with deep pitting irony.

2271
02:31:46,515 --> 02:31:51,750
Pakistan pulled out two chits from his pocket, one from Saudi Arabia and one from America.

2272
02:31:51,830 --> 02:31:55,837
As Paxan was about to recite the content of those chits,

2273
02:31:55,917 --> 02:31:58,650
it felt two bug bites on its legs.

2274
02:31:58,730 --> 02:32:04,150
He moved his pants and found two insects biting him, named TTP and BLA.

2275
02:32:04,230 --> 02:32:09,650
Paxan stood there for a second, his grin slowly freezing into an uncomfortable stance.

2276
02:32:09,730 --> 02:32:11,450
You may sit down, the teacher said.

2277
02:32:11,530 --> 02:32:18,180
As Paxan was sitting, Afghanistan, the biggest trouble maker of the class, discreetly jabbed a sharp metal compass.

2278
02:32:18,260 --> 02:32:20,499
right into the back of Pakistan's seat.

2279
02:32:20,579 --> 02:32:31,553
Pakistan jumped and immediately requested his friends Saudi USA and China for help but all three of them pretended to be absolutely pensive in their books.

2280
02:32:31,633 --> 02:32:34,475
Fourth period, career counseling.

2281
02:32:34,555 --> 02:32:39,570
The teacher asked everyone to write down their core competency for the next decade.

2282
02:32:39,650 --> 02:32:45,040
Singapore, financial hub, South Korea, innovation and tech, Vietnam, global manufacturing,

2283
02:32:45,120 --> 02:32:46,593
UAE, Tourism and Logistics.

2284
02:32:46,673 --> 02:32:48,398
Pakistan stood up confidently.

2285
02:32:48,478 --> 02:32:50,146
I was destined for greatness.

2286
02:32:50,226 --> 02:32:51,837
I have a strategic location.

2287
02:32:51,917 --> 02:32:54,122
The teacher noted it down.

2288
02:32:54,202 --> 02:32:56,791
Location is a setting, Pakistan, not a skill.

2289
02:32:56,871 --> 02:32:59,597
What skills have you acquired since last term?

2290
02:32:59,677 --> 02:33:00,057
Silence.

2291
02:33:00,137 --> 02:33:02,182
Pakistan quickly shifted gear.

2292
02:33:02,262 --> 02:33:07,864
Did you know my grandfather was the best debater in the entire district in nineteen forty-seven?

2293
02:33:07,944 --> 02:33:10,927
Let me tell you about his speeches.

2294
02:33:11,007 --> 02:33:12,790
The teacher gently interrupted.

2295
02:33:13,240 --> 02:33:16,920
I'm not even asking about your grandfather, I'm asking about you.

2296
02:33:17,000 --> 02:33:24,040
Pakistan zoned out as it got too distracted looking at two kids fighting outside Israel and Palestine.

2297
02:33:24,120 --> 02:33:27,800
Fifth period, moral science and ethics.

2298
02:33:27,880 --> 02:33:33,320
