2310
02:34:06,319 --> 02:34:07,130
Question one.

2311
02:34:07,490 --> 02:34:13,730
Name the most morally bankrupt nation in the world and justify your answer. Pakistan's answer, Israel.

2312
02:34:13,810 --> 02:34:18,322
Reasoning, massive human rights violation, brutally illegal occupation,

2313
02:34:18,402 --> 02:34:22,040
illegal occupations and absolute contempt for human life.

2314
02:34:22,840 --> 02:34:27,723
Propose global resolution, immediate international military intervention,

2315
02:34:27,803 --> 02:34:32,620
global sanctions, absolute economic boycott and public trial at the hog.

2316
02:34:33,330 --> 02:34:35,200
Question two, what is your country's?

2317
02:34:35,280 --> 02:34:40,320
official stance on peaceful public protest. Pakistan's answer, absolute zero tolerance.

2318
02:34:41,900 --> 02:34:45,517
If my own citizens assemble peacefully in Islamabad, Balochistan,

2319
02:34:45,597 --> 02:34:50,407
KPK or Azad Kashmir to ask for basic rights, legislative representation, clean water,

2320
02:34:50,487 --> 02:34:55,583
electricity, internet or missing family members, I tear gas them.

2321
02:34:55,663 --> 02:35:01,780
Cut off the internet, label them anti-state, foreign agents and throw them into the sea.

2322
02:35:01,860 --> 02:35:06,980
them into military trial dungeons. Question number three, is there a contradiction between

2323
02:35:07,060 --> 02:35:13,620
your answers to question one and question two? Pakistan's answer, no. When foreign nations do it,

2324
02:35:13,700 --> 02:35:18,500
it is a crime against humanity. When I do it to my own people, it's maintaining internal order.

2325
02:35:19,380 --> 02:35:24,420
Question number four, is peaceful assembly and political dissent a fundamental human right?

2326
02:35:25,140 --> 02:35:29,280
Pakistan's answer, only when done by Palestinians, Indian Kashmiris.

2327
02:35:29,360 --> 02:35:30,772
or students in London.

2328
02:35:30,852 --> 02:35:36,980
On my own soil, it is a terror threat punishable by tear gas and anti-terrorism charges.

2329
02:35:37,660 --> 02:35:38,706
Question number five.

2330
02:35:38,786 --> 02:35:40,556
Explain the concept of democracy.

2331
02:35:40,636 --> 02:35:41,521
Pakistan's answer.

2332
02:35:41,601 --> 02:35:49,080
A ceremonial sport where citizens line up to vote for four hours so the military can announce the predetermined winner four days later.

2333
02:35:49,160 --> 02:35:56,160
Question number six. What are the two core pillars that define your moral compass? Pakistan hesitated.

2334
02:35:56,800 --> 02:36:00,332
He tapped his pen against his chin, glanced at Saudi Arabia's wallet,

2335
02:36:00,412 --> 02:36:05,618
looked toward Washington, had a brief eye contact with China, and then quickly scribbled,

2336
02:36:05,698 --> 02:36:07,950
Money, number one, money, number two, Islam.

2337
02:36:09,590 --> 02:36:13,032
The teacher walked up to the aisle, collecting the papers.

2338
02:36:13,112 --> 02:36:17,169
She paused at Pakistan's desk, reading his answers right off the page.

2339
02:36:17,249 --> 02:36:19,510
A heavy, ironic smile crossed her face.

2340
02:36:19,590 --> 02:36:22,220
